---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | ALMA AI">


<main class="about">


<section class="hero">

<h1>
Beyond Answers.<br/>
Towards Understanding.
</h1>


<p class="lead">
ALMA AI is an independent research initiative exploring a new generation
of artificial intelligence designed to understand people, relationships,
and human decision patterns.
</p>


<p>
The project began in 2025 from a simple question:
why do intelligent people still struggle to understand themselves
and each other?
</p>

</section>





<section>

<h2>
Beyond Large Language Models
</h2>


<p>
Modern AI systems based on Large Language Models (LLMs) are powerful tools
for generating information, solving problems, and assisting human tasks.
</p>


<p>
However, most AI interactions are based on individual conversations.
They respond to prompts, but they do not create a continuously developing
understanding of a person's identity, values, and behavioral patterns.
</p>



<div class="comparison">


<div>

<h3>
Traditional AI
</h3>


<p>
Question → Answer
</p>

<p>
Context is temporary.
</p>

<p>
Focus:
information generation.
</p>

</div>



<div>

<h3>
ALMA Vision
</h3>


<p>
Interaction → Observation → Understanding
</p>


<p>
Context becomes structured knowledge.
</p>

<p>
Focus:
human understanding.
</p>

</div>


</div>


</section>







<section>

<h2>
ALMA is not another chatbot
</h2>


<p>
ALMA is not designed to simply generate more answers.
</p>


<p>
The goal is to explore a persistent cognitive model —
an AI system that can develop a structured understanding of a person
through meaningful interactions over time.
</p>


<p>
Instead of asking:
</p>


<blockquote>
"What answer should AI generate?"
</blockquote>


<p>
ALMA asks:
</p>


<blockquote>
"What does this person value, how do they think,
and what patterns influence their decisions?"
</blockquote>


</section>







<section>

<h2>
How ALMA Thinks
</h2>


<div class="architecture">


<div>
Human Interaction

<span>
Experiences, conversations, decisions
</span>

</div>


<div>
Observations

<span>
Extracting meaningful patterns
</span>

</div>


<div>
Structured Memory

<span>
Organized understanding over time
</span>

</div>


<div>
Insights

<span>
Helping people understand themselves and others
</span>

</div>


</div>


</section>








<section>

<h2>
Understanding Human Compatibility
</h2>


<p>
The first research direction of ALMA focuses on long-term compatibility:
understanding why some relationships become stronger over time,
while others fail despite attraction and emotional connection.
</p>


<p>
Future systems based on these principles may help people understand
potential partners, friendships, and important human connections
through deeper psychological patterns rather than superficial matching.
</p>


</section>







<section>

<h2>
Future Possibilities
</h2>


<ul>

<li>
Finding partners based on deeper psychological compatibility.
</li>

<li>
Discovering friendships based on shared values and perspectives.
</li>

<li>
Improving professional collaboration and team formation.
</li>

<li>
Creating personalized AI systems for self-reflection and decision making.
</li>

<li>
Building new ways for humans to understand themselves and each other.
</li>

</ul>


</section>







<section class="closing">


<h2>
The ALMA Principle
</h2>


<p>
The future of artificial intelligence should not only be about generating
more answers.
</p>


<p>
It should be about creating better understanding between people.
</p>


</section>



</main>






